# Acme Tickets repositories

Fictional company. Replace with your own repos.

## Repositories

| Repo | What it is | Layout | Test command | TDD? |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `acme-api-orders` | Orders, refunds, seat holds (REST API) | `resources/<feature>/{queries,commands,handlers,models}/` | `npm test` (unit), `npm run test:coverage` | yes |
| `acme-api-events` | Events, venues, schedules (REST API) | same as above | `npm test`, `npm run test:coverage` | yes |
| `acme-api-payments` | Payment provider integration (REST API) | same as above | `npm test`, `npm run test:coverage` | yes |
| `acme-web-app` | Box-office web app (server-rendered + Vue) | `app/modules/<feature>/{queries,commands}/` | `npm run test:unit` | no, write tests after, same task |
| `acme-reports-app` | Reporting front end | `app/modules/<feature>/` | `npm run test:unit` | no |
| `acme-ui-kit` | Shared UI components (published as a git tag) | `src/components/` | `npm test` | yes |
| `acme-db-translations` | Translation keys and their migrations | `migrations/` | none; migrations are not run as tests | n/a |

The repos listed as "no" under TDD are the ones in `skipRedGreen` of `kit.config.json`. The one with no tests is in `noCoverageRepos`.

## Pre-commit commands

Run in the repo you changed, in this order: `npm run lint`, then the test command above. Fix failures before committing.

## Context sources for discovery and summaries

- Product docs: https://docs.acme-tickets.example/product
- Technical docs (APIs, webhooks): https://docs.acme-tickets.example/api
- Developer wiki: https://docs.acme-tickets.example/wiki
- Sandbox for visual checks: https://sandbox.acme-tickets.example (ask for credentials; never write them down)

## Branches

The integration branch is `main`. Feature branches are named `<ticket-id>-<short-title>`.

